# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test
*.prof

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
.idea/
.vscode/

# Others
gossip*.txt

# graphify knowledge graph. Only the four artifacts at graphify-out/ root are tracked:
# GRAPH_REPORT.md, graph.html, graph.json, manifest.json. The rest is machine-local
# scratch (extraction cache, interpreter path, cumulative token cost) or a dated
# snapshot each rebuild leaves behind, mostly a duplicate of graph.json.
graphify-out/cache/
graphify-out/.graphify_*
graphify-out/cost.json
graphify-out/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]/
